      <!-- The WESP glyphs these SLDs use, redrawn as native marks (glyph
           shapes read from the WESP font's own outlines): glyph 101 is an X,
           repeated along the mt4 lines every 25 px after its own 18
           (LineStyle_Pattern, PLength 43), colored by coordination level;
           glyph 58 is a right-pointing block arrow, of which the head
           (a triangle turned 90 degrees) is drawn on the mt1 points. -->
